.TH "si" "1" "2026\-11\-02" "v0.0.1" "General Commands Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
si \- parse, convert, and format physical quantities using SI units
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBsi\fR [OPTIONS] VALUE
.br
\fBsi\fR \-\-completions SHELL
.br
\fBsi\fR \-\-version
.br
\fBsi\fR \-\-help
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBsi\fR is a command\-line utility for parsing, converting, and formatting physical quantities expressed using the International System of Units (SI).\&
.PP
A quantity consists of a numeric value followed by a unit expression.\& 
Unit expressions support multiplication, division, exponentiation, and grouping using ASCII infix notation.\&
.PP
Quantities can be converted to a specified target unit, with dimensional compatibility checked during conversion.\&
Output can be formatted in several representations, including UTF\-8 encoded symbols, plain text, JSON, and LaTeX.\&
.PP
Numeric output supports configurable decimal precision and notation, including general, fixed\-point, scientific, and E\-notation.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-notation\fR NOTATION
.RS 4
Set numeric notation.\& Supported values are \fBgeneral\fR, \fBfixed\fR, \fBscientific\fR, \fBe\fR, and \fBE\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR FORMAT
.RS 4
Set output format.\& Supported values are \fBascii\fR, \fButf\fR, \fBjson\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-precision\fR INTEGER
.RS 4
Set decimal precision (default: 3).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-unit\fR UNIT
.RS 4
Convert the quantity to the specified target unit representation.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-completions\fR SHELL
.RS 4
Generate shell completions for Bash or Zsh.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Display version information.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Display help information.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH UNIT FORMATTING SYNTAX
.PP
The `\-u`, `\-\-unit` option accepts a restricted syntax for specifying the target unit representation.\& 
Expressions must use ASCII unit symbols (eg.\& kg, us, ohm) and the following operators:
.PP
\fB\fRSymbols\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
Multiplication       *
.IP \(bu 4
Division             /
.IP \(bu 4
Exponentiation       \(ha
.IP \(bu 4
Positive exponent    +
.IP \(bu 4
Negative exponent    \-
.IP \(bu 4
Grouping             ()
.PD
.PP
\fB\fRValid examples\fB\fR\fB
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
kg*m/s\(ha2
.IP \(bu 4
mol/L
.IP \(bu 4
uF/cm\(ha2
.IP \(bu 4
kW\fRh
.IP \(bu 4
m\(ha3/s
.PD
.PP
Unicode operator variants, superscript exponents, alternative multiplication symbols, and alternative spellings of unit symbols are not supported.\&
.PP
.SH UNIT PARSING SYNTAX
.PP
The parser accepts numeric quantities using fixed\-point or scientific notation.\&
.PP
Unit expressions are parsed more permissively than the format syntax in order to accommodate common variations in notation.\&
.PP
\fB\fRValid examples\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
uohm*m\(ha\-2  \-> µΩ·m⁻²
.IP \(bu 4
μohm*m**\-2 \-> µΩ·m⁻²
.IP \(bu 4
µΩ·m⁻²     \-> µΩ·m⁻²
.IP \(bu 4
uΩ×m\(ha−2    \-> µΩ·m⁻²
.IP \(bu 4
μΩ⋅m⁻²     \-> µΩ·m⁻²
.PD
.PP
In addition to ASCII representations, the parser accepts the following UTF\-8 encoded characters:
.PP
\fB\fRMultiplication\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
ASTERISK                     (U+002A)
.IP \(bu 4
ASTERISK OPERATOR            (U+2217)
.IP \(bu 4
STAR OPERATOR                (U+22C6)
.IP \(bu 4
MULTIPLICATION SIGN          (U+00D7)
.IP \(bu 4
MIDDLE DOT                   (U+00B7)
.IP \(bu 4
HYPHENATION POINT            (U+2027)
.IP \(bu 4
BULLET OPERATOR              (U+2219)
.IP \(bu 4
DOT OPERATOR                 (U+22C5)
.IP \(bu 4
LATIN LETTER SINOLOGICAL DOT (U+A78F)
.PD
.PP
\fB\fRExponentiation\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
CIRCUMFLEX ACCENT            (U+005E)
.IP \(bu 4
ASTERISK ASTERISK            (U+002A U+002A)
.PD
.PP
\fB\fRSuperscript digits\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT ZERO             (U+2070)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT ONE              (U+00B9)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT TWO              (U+00B2)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT THREE            (U+00B3)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT FOUR             (U+2074)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT FIVE             (U+2075)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT SIX              (U+2076)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT SEVEN            (U+2077)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT EIGHT            (U+2078)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT NINE             (U+2079)
.PD
.PP
\fB\fRExponent signs\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
PLUS SIGN                    (U+002B)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT PLUS SIGN        (U+207A)
.IP \(bu 4
HYPHEN\-MINUS                 (U+002D)
.IP \(bu 4
HYPHEN                       (U+2010)
.IP \(bu 4
MINUS SIGN                   (U+2212)
.IP \(bu 4
SUPERSCRIPT MINUS            (U+207B)
.PD
.PP
\fB\fRGrouping\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
LEFT PARENTHESIS             (U+0028)
.IP \(bu 4
RIGHT PARENTHESIS            (U+0029)
.IP \(bu 4
LEFT CURLY BRACKET           (U+007B)
.IP \(bu 4
RIGHT CURLY BRACKET          (U+007D)
.PD
.PP
\fB\fRMicro prefix\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
MICRO SIGN                   (U+00B5)
.IP \(bu 4
GREEK SMALL LETTER MU        (U+03BC)
.PD
.PP
\fB\fROhm\fB\fR
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
`OHM SIGN`                   (U+2126)
.IP \(bu 4
`GREEK CAPITAL LETTER OMEGA` (U+03A9)
.PD
.PP
These variations are accepted when parsing input quantities.\& They do not necessarily apply to target unit expressions or determine how units are formatted in output.\&
.PP
Whitespace is permitted between expression components.\&
.PP
